# The golden wire snapshot (T7.7) is compared BYTE FOR BYTE against what the
# encoder emits, so a checkout must not rewrite it: core.autocrlf=true would hand
# the test CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux, and the guard would then be pinning one
# wire on one platform and a different one on the other. -text disables both
# normalisation directions AND the EOL conversion for that file only.
#
# Nothing else is listed here on purpose: this file is the repository's first, so
# adding `* text=auto` alongside it would silently change the EOL handling of every
# tracked file (the worktree currently mixes CRLF and LF working-tree files over an
# LF index, decided by core.autocrlf). The wire snapshot is the one file whose bytes
# ARE the contract; leave the rest as they were.
*.ndjson -text
